---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Content as Poster } from '../../content/poster.md';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const gh = 'https://github.com/gitmick/asif-jam/blob/main/examples/trees-and-culture';
const kton = `${base}/kton`;

// Every file the chain read or wrote is served under /kton/files at the bytes a signed foton
// recorded, so the table below is not a description of the chain — it is the chain.
const chain = [
  ['01-trees.R',       'the tree register → 23 districts × 75 covariates', ['district-trees.csv', 'species-key.csv']],
  ['02-funding.R',     'culture subsidies per district',                   ['district-funding.csv']],
  ['03-join.R',        'one table, 23 rows',                               ['district-table.csv']],
  ['04-search.R',      '142 506 models fitted, the best one reported',     ['best-model.csv', 'predictions.csv', 'model-fit.png']],
  ['05-advice.R',      'coefficients → planting instructions',             ['planting-advice.csv']],
  ['06-does-it-hold.R','three validation checks',                          ['validation.csv', 'permutation.png']],
  ['07-poster.R',      'the poster, as markdown',                          ['poster.md']],
];
---
<Base title="Fell the oaks, fund the theatre — As-If Science Jam"
      description="A worked example for the jam: a poster with an R² of 0.906 in which every number is correct and the conclusion is nonsense. The whole chain is published, signed, and refuted.">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Source+Serif+4:wght@400;600;700&family=Source+Sans+3:wght@400;600&display=swap" />
  </Fragment>

  <a href={`${base}/examples`} class="font-mono text-[12px] text-muted no-underline hover:text-accent">← examples</a>
  <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[.16em] text-accent">Worked example</p>
  <h1 class="mt-3 text-[clamp(1.9rem,4.4vw,2.9rem)] font-semibold leading-tight tracking-[-.022em]">
    Fell the oaks, fund the theatre
  </h1>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Two unmodified files from Vienna's open data portal — 232 619 street trees and every subsidy
    the city paid in 2024 — produce a model with an <strong class="font-medium text-ink">R² of
    0.906</strong> and a planting policy. Every number on the poster below is correct. You can
    re-run the seven scripts and get the same figures back. The conclusion is still nonsense, and
    the whole example exists so you can see exactly where the nonsense enters.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
    <a href={`${gh}/TASK.md`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
       class="rounded border border-line px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[13px] text-muted no-underline hover:border-accent hover:text-accent">The task ↗</a>
    <a href={`${gh}/04-search.R`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
       class="rounded border border-line px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[13px] text-muted no-underline hover:border-accent hover:text-accent">04-search.R ↗</a>
    <a href={`${gh}/06-does-it-hold.R`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
       class="rounded border border-line px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[13px] text-muted no-underline hover:border-accent hover:text-accent">06-does-it-hold.R ↗</a>
    <a href={`${base}/datasets/vienna-baumkataster`}
       class="rounded border border-line px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[13px] text-muted no-underline hover:border-accent hover:text-accent">The tree register</a>
    <a href={`${base}/datasets/wien-foerderbericht`}
       class="rounded border border-line px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[13px] text-muted no-underline hover:border-accent hover:text-accent">The subsidy report</a>
  </div>

  <!-- ─── the poster ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="mt-10">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2 border-b border-line pb-2">
      <h2 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[.14em] text-faint">The poster</h2>
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] text-faint">
        written by <a href={`${gh}/07-poster.R`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-muted no-underline hover:text-accent">07-poster.R</a>
        as <a href={`${kton}/files/poster.md`} class="text-muted no-underline hover:text-accent">markdown</a>,
        rendered here
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="poster-sheet mt-5"><Poster /></div>
    <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed text-faint">
      Hover the figure. The lens checks it against a signed lineage in your browser — nothing is
      uploaded — and clicking it opens the seven steps that produced it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── the refutation ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="mt-12 border-t border-line pt-10">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[.14em] text-accent">Where the nonsense enters</p>
    <h2 class="mt-2 max-w-[30ch] text-[clamp(1.25rem,2.6vw,1.7rem)] font-semibold leading-snug tracking-[-.012em]">
      Not in the arithmetic — in a sentence no results table contains
    </h2>
    <blockquote class="mt-5 max-w-[66ch] border-l-2 border-accent pl-5 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      We ranked ~100 covariates by correlation, kept the thirty strongest, fitted
      <strong class="font-medium text-ink">every combination of five</strong> against
      <strong class="font-medium text-ink">23 data points</strong>, and reported the best.
    </blockquote>
    <p class="mt-5 max-w-[66ch] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      That is 142 506 models. With 23 observations, a search that wide finds a good fit in
      anything at all. <code class="rounded bg-accent/10 px-1 font-mono text-[.9em] text-ink">06-does-it-hold.R</code>
      measures how much:
    </p>

    <table class="mt-6 w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
      <thead><tr>
        <th class="border-b border-line py-2 pr-4 text-left font-semibold text-ink">Check</th>
        <th class="border-b border-line py-2 text-right font-semibold text-ink">Value</th>
      </tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="border-b border-line py-2 pr-4 text-muted">fitted on all 23 districts</td>
            <td class="border-b border-line py-2 text-right font-mono text-ink">R² = 0.906</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="border-b border-line py-2 pr-4 text-muted">leave one district out, same five predictors</td>
            <td class="border-b border-line py-2 text-right font-mono text-muted">Q² = 0.772</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="border-b border-line py-2 pr-4 text-muted">leave one district out, <strong class="font-medium text-ink">redoing the search each time</strong></td>
            <td class="border-b border-line py-2 text-right font-mono text-accent">Q² = −0.184</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="border-b border-line py-2 pr-4 text-muted">the same search on randomly shuffled funding</td>
            <td class="border-b border-line py-2 text-right font-mono text-accent">R² mean 0.760, best 0.868</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="mt-7 grid gap-7 sm:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.1fr)] sm:items-start">
      <p class="max-w-[52ch] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        The last two lines are the whole story. A negative <em class="not-italic text-ink">Q²</em>
        means the model predicts a held-out district <em>worse than the average would have</em>.
        And when the funding column is shuffled into noise, the same search still reaches 0.868
        against the reported 0.906 — so the fit is not evidence of a relationship. It is what the
        search returns.
      </p>
      <figure class="m-0">
        <img class="lens w-full rounded border border-line bg-white" loading="lazy"
             src={`${kton}/files/permutation.png`}
             alt="Histogram of the R² the same search reaches on randomly shuffled funding figures, with the reported 0.906 marked." />
        <figcaption class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed text-faint">
          What the search finds in pure noise. The red line is the poster's R².
          Produced by <a href={`${gh}/06-does-it-hold.R`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-muted no-underline hover:text-accent">06-does-it-hold.R</a>.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 max-w-[66ch] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Everything before those two lines is reproducible, and that is exactly the point the jam is
      making: <strong class="font-medium text-ink">reproducible is not the same as true</strong>,
      and no amount of checking the first buys you the second.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── the chain ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="mt-12 border-t border-line pt-10">
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[.14em] text-accent">All of it, by hash</p>
    <h2 class="mt-2 text-[clamp(1.25rem,2.6vw,1.7rem)] font-semibold leading-snug tracking-[-.012em]">
      The chain
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Seven steps, each one a signed foton over the bytes it read and the bytes it wrote. Every
      file below is served here at exactly those bytes, so you can fetch one, hash it yourself,
      and get the value the lineage records.
    </p>

    <ul class="mt-6 list-none divide-y divide-line overflow-hidden rounded border border-line">
      {chain.map(([script, what, outs]) => (
        <li class="grid gap-1 bg-panel p-4 sm:grid-cols-[13rem_minmax(0,1fr)] sm:gap-5">
          <a href={`${kton}/files/${script}`} class="font-mono text-[13px] text-accent no-underline hover:underline">{script}</a>
          <div>
            <p class="text-[14px] leading-snug text-muted">{what}</p>
            <p class="mt-1.5 flex flex-wrap gap-x-3 gap-y-1 font-mono text-[11px]">
              {outs.map(o => <a href={`${kton}/files/${o}`} class="text-faint no-underline hover:text-accent">{o}</a>)}
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-5 max-w-[66ch] font-mono text-[12px] leading-relaxed text-faint">
      The one file not served here is the tree register itself: 53 MB, and a <em class="not-italic text-muted">live</em>
      register, so two fetches are not the same file. The lineage carries its hash, and
      <a href={`${gh}/01-trees.R`} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-muted no-underline hover:text-accent">01-trees.R</a>
      falls back to the repository's later snapshot — which does not reproduce these numbers exactly,
      and says so when it runs.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href={`${kton}/viewer.html?union=data/trees-and-culture/union.json&keys=data/trees-and-culture/keys.json&names=data/trees-and-culture/names.json`}
         class="rounded border border-accent bg-accent/10 px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[13px] text-accent no-underline hover:bg-accent/20">Open the lineage →</a>
      <a href={`${kton}/data/trees-and-culture/union.json`}
         class="rounded border border-line px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[13px] text-muted no-underline hover:border-accent hover:text-accent">union.json</a>
      <a href="https://kton.dev" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
         class="rounded border border-line px-4 py-2 font-mono text-[13px] text-muted no-underline hover:border-accent hover:text-accent">What kton is ↗</a>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-7 rounded border border-line bg-panel p-5">
      <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[.14em] text-faint">A signed claim, attached to the poster's bytes</p>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-[70ch] leading-relaxed text-muted">
        <span class="text-ink">Reproducible, and wrong.</span> Every figure on this poster
        recomputes from the recorded inputs. The conclusion does not survive validation:
        leave-one-out that redoes the variable search each time gives Q² = −0.184, worse than
        predicting the mean, and the same search run on randomly shuffled funding figures still
        reaches R² = 0.868 against the reported 0.906.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-[11px] text-faint">
        pav:reviewedBy · CN=As-If Science Jam, Schmiede Hallein 2026 · keyid 661531a51d0c6a2b
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ─── run it ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="mt-12 border-t border-line pt-10">
    <h2 class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[.14em] text-faint">Run it yourself</h2>
    <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded border border-line bg-panel p-5 font-mono text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted"><code>cp -r examples/trees-and-culture work/yourname-trees
cd work/yourname-trees
Rscript 01-trees.R && Rscript 02-funding.R && Rscript 03-join.R
Rscript 04-search.R && Rscript 05-advice.R && Rscript 06-does-it-hold.R && Rscript 07-poster.R</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <code class="rounded bg-accent/10 px-1 font-mono text-[.9em] text-ink">out/</code> already
      holds the results, so you can start at any step. Then do the same manoeuvre on your own
      dataset — once you have seen it here, you will recognise it in a paper.
    </p>
  </section>

  <script is:inline src={`${kton}/lens.js`}
          data-planktons={`${kton}/data/trees-and-culture/union.json`}
          data-viewer={`${kton}/viewer.html`}
          data-logo={`${kton}/logo.png`}
          data-selector=".poster-sheet img, img.lens"></script>
</Base>
